sentences.text:
Having heard the learned advocates for the parties and perusing the material placed on record and taking into consideration the facts of the case, nature of allegations, gravity of offences, role attributed to the accused, without discussing the evidence in detail, at this stage, I am inclined to grant anticipatory bail to the applicant.
6. This Court has considered following aspects,
(i) applicant is not the main accused nor he is named in the FIR;

( ii) the role alleged against present applicant is that when the main accused ran away with the complainant, he arranged for an advocate and Maulvi for solemnizing the marriage of accused Riyaz and complainant and that he provided a jacket and LC of the main accused Riyaz;
(iii) except for the aforesaid role, prima R/CR.MA/4291/2022 ORDER DATED: 19/06/2023 facie,
as per investigation which has been carried out till date, learned APP could not point out any further role of the present applicant;
(iv) applicant is arraigned as an accused on the basis of statement of co-accused;
(v) no past antecedent is attributed to the present applicant and the applicant has shown willingness to cooperate with the investigation;
(vi) pursuant to the order dated 23.02.2022 applicant was protected and he was directed to appear before Investigating Officer on 28.02.2022 which indicates that though more than one year has passed, there is nothing which can be pointed out by the IO that applicant is not cooperating with the investigation.

The applicant is ordered to be released on bail in the event of arrest in connection with FIR Part-A 11191020211185 of 2021 registered with Vastrapur Police Station, Dist.Ahmedabad on executing a personal bond of Rs.10,000/- (Rupees Ten Thousand Only) with one surety of like amount on the following conditions that the applicant:
R/CR.MA/4291/2022 ORDER DATED: 19/06/2023 (a) shall cooperate with the investigation and make themselves available for interrogation whenever required;
(b) shall remain present at concerned Police Station on 26.06.2023 between 11.00 a.m. and 2.00 p.m.;
(c) shall not directly or indirectly make any inducement, threat or promise to any person acquainted with the fact of the case so as to dissuade him from disclosing such facts to the court or to any police officer;
(d) shall not obstruct or hamper the police investigation and not to play mischief with the evidence collected or yet to be collected by the police;
(e) shall at the time of execution of bond, furnish the address to the investigating officer and the court concerned and shall not change residence till the final disposal of the case till further orders;
R/CR.MA/4291/2022 ORDER DATED: 19/06/2023 (f) shall not leave India without the permission of the concerned trial court and if having passport shall deposit the same before the concerned trial court within a week; and (g) it would be open to the Investigating Officer to file an application for remand if he considers it proper and just and the learned Magistrate would decide it on merits;
10.

